-- title:
--   Supersingular completed local ring descends to an unramified base
-- statement:
--   Fix a discrete valuation domain $A$, a prime $q$, a natural number $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$; assume $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ while $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$, and that the residue field of $A$ is finite. Assume the three equivariance hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL`: for every $A$-algebra $T$, a Weierstrass curve over $T$ and a variable change $C$, the condition [`ModularCurve.IsGamma1Point`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma1Pow.html#L10) for $\ell_g$ (the point $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the curve equation, is a root of $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) is preserved by `LevelPData.variableChange`; the condition [`ModularCurve.IsGamma0PowAt`](def/ModularCurve_WeierstrassGamma0Pow.html#L55) for $p^k$ (two-torsion kernel form if $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic generator-kernel conditions on degree, leading coefficient and divisibility of division polynomials) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` is preserved under the same twisting. Fix group laws $\mathcal G$ on projective Weierstrass models over $A$-algebras which are chord-and-tangent (compatible with the affine point group after base change to fields) and have the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal T$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases satisfying the section-transport compatibilities, and the two pinning hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO` asserting, for every $A$-algebra $T$, the existence of graded ring homomorphisms of the projective-model coordinate rings realising a variable change, respectively a coefficient change along an $A$-algebra map, with the irrelevant-ideal condition. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package (an $A$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point `univ` representing the point functor) for the datum `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …`, whose level structures are a $\Gamma_0(M')$-structure given by generator-kernel polynomials at each prime power dividing $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, subject to the link condition `IsGamma1Link`; assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A$. Let $\mathfrak p$ be a minimal prime of $B_0$. Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, let $\varepsilon \in A$ be a unit with $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon q$, and let $\zeta \in A$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let `xr` be a raw point over $B_0$ whose class in the quotient by the variable-change relation is $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$, let $x$ be a maximal ideal of $B_0/\mathfrak p$ containing the image of the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $F_0$ be a formal group over $(B_0/\mathfrak p)/x$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law `formalGroupLawFixed` of the reduction of `xr.curve` modulo $\mathfrak p$ and then $x$, such that the $q$-th iterate series `F₀.nthSeries q` equals a unit times $X^{q\cdot q}$. Then there exist a discrete valuation domain $A_0$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$ and whose residue field is finite, equivariance hypotheses, group laws $\mathcal G_0$ chord-and-tangent with origin identity, a section transport $\mathcal T_0$, and pinning hypotheses over $A_0$, a fine moduli package $P_u$ for `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q …` with $P_u.B_0$ of finite type over $A_0$, a raw point `xu` representing $P_u.\mathrm{univ}$, a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_u$ of $P_u.B_0$ containing the image of $q$, and a formal group $F_{0u}$ over $P_u.B_0/\mathfrak m_u$ equal to the fixed formal group law of the reduction of `xu.curve` with `F₀u.nthSeries q` again a unit times $X^{q \cdot q}$, for which the adic completion of $B_0/\mathfrak p$ at $x$ and the adic completion of $P_u.B_0$ at $\mathfrak m_u$ are isomorphic as rings.
--
--   This is the descent step which replaces the base $A$, containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity and hence ramified over $\mathbb{Z}_{(q)}$, by an unramified discrete valuation ring $A_0$ with maximal ideal $(q)$: the completed local ring at a supersingular point of a component of the fine moduli ring for the $\Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ level datum with Drinfeld $q$-basis is recognised as the completed local ring of a universal package over $A_0$. It feeds the reducedness statement for the residue field tensored with such a completion.
